Operational handover occurs when responsibility for an Azure environment moves from one team to another, such as from project implementation teams to cloud operations teams.

A successful handover should include:

* Architecture documentation
* Access credentials
* Operational runbooks
* Backup procedures
* Monitoring configuration
* Incident escalation contacts
* Known issues
* Maintenance schedules

# Real-Life Example:
For example, after completing an Azure migration project, implementation engineers formally transfer operational responsibility to the infrastructure support team.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is managed service providers delivering completed Azure environments to customer operations teams.

A structured handover reduces operational confusion and improves service continuity.
